# Docker build exclusions for the conscious-subconscious service image.
#
# WARNING — placement matters. Docker reads `.dockerignore` from the BUILD
# CONTEXT root, which for this project is the repository root (see the `context:`
# key in docker-compose.yml and `-f deploy/docker/Dockerfile ... .` in the
# Makefile). A `.dockerignore` in this directory is therefore NOT consulted by
# the daemon; the equivalent file has to live at the repository root. It is kept
# here as the editable source of truth for that file and so the exclusions are
# documented next to the Dockerfile that depends on them. See deploy/README.md.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Node / web workspaces: never part of the Python image
node_modules
**/node_modules
apps/*/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python virtualenvs and caches
.venv
venv
env
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
coverage.xml

# Local runtime state and generated artefacts
out
runs
tmp
*.sqlite3
*.db
sbom.json
sbom.spdx.json
deploy/out
site

# Secrets: never copied into an image layer, even a throwaway one
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Editors and OS noise
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documentation and research material are not needed to run the service
docs
research
marketing
media
site
mkdocs.yml
